+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for contributing to `awesome-best-ai-tools-for-recruiters-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+- Every tool must have a public `github.com` repository URL.
+- No proprietary SaaS tools.
+- The repository must be relevant to recruiters, ATS workflows, resume screening, candidate pipelines, hiring analytics, job boards, or recruiting automation.
+- Include the tool name, GitHub URL, stars, primary language, license, and last commit date.
+- If the repo is early-stage, abandoned, or clearly a prototype, note that honestly.
+- If a category has fewer than 5 credible repositories, document it as a gap instead of padding the list.
+
+## Pull Request Checklist
+
+- Confirm the repository is public on GitHub.
+- Confirm the tool is open source.
+- Confirm the license is visible on GitHub.
+- Confirm the metadata is current when you submit the PR.
+- Confirm the description reflects the repository README and not marketing copy from another site.
+- Confirm the entry format matches existing sections in `README.md`.
+
+## Suggested Entry Format
+
+```md
+#### [Tool Name](https://github.com/username/repo)
+> **Description:** Short summary based on the GitHub README. Include what it does, key features, licensing, stars, language, and maintenance context.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/username/repo](https://github.com/username/repo)
+- **Stars:** 123 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** 2026-03-31
+- **Category:** tag1, tag2
+- **Best for:** specific recruiter use case
+```
+
+## Quality Standard
+
+This repo prefers fewer strong entries over many weak ones. If a project is only loosely related to recruiting, do not add it.
