+### Gaps Worth Noting
+
+The recruiting OSS landscape is still uneven.
+
+- **Interview automation:** Fewer than 5 strong GitHub-native repos surfaced that are clearly recruiter-first, actively maintained, and fully open-source.
+- **Talent sourcing assistants:** Fewer than 5 strong repos surfaced that are clearly built for sourcers or recruiter outbound workflows instead of job-seeker automation.
+- **Recruiter CRM / candidate rediscovery:** Public GitHub coverage exists, but the quality drop-off after the top few repos is sharp.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for recruiters in 2026?
+The strongest options in this list are `Resume-Matcher` for AI-assisted resume tailoring, `OpenCATS`, `SpotAxis`, and `YAWIK` for ATS foundations, and `OpenResume` plus `pyresparser` for parsing and ATS-readability workflows.
+
+### Are there any free self-hosted AI recruiting tools on GitHub?
+Yes. `Resume-Matcher`, `JobSync`, `OpenResume`, `SpotAxis`, `OpenCATS`, and `YAWIK` are all public GitHub repositories that can be self-hosted or forked for internal use.
+
+### Which GitHub repos help recruiters screen resumes against job descriptions?
+The best fits are `Resume-Matcher`, `acenji/ats`, `KalyanM45/Application-Tracking-System`, `next-hire-ai`, and `JobSync`. They all expose some combination of comparison, scoring, keyword matching, or AI-generated feedback.
+
+### What is the best open source ATS on GitHub for small recruiting teams?
+For small teams, `OpenCATS`, `SpotAxis`, and `YAWIK` are the strongest foundations. `hire-smart` and `jugglehire.com` are also worth reviewing if interview scheduling or simpler workflows matter more than deep ATS customization.
+
+### Are there open source GitHub alternatives to recruiter SaaS job boards?
+Yes. `Riminder/open-jobboard`, `aschmelyun/laravel-job-board`, `golang-cafe/job-board`, `Abdullah-moiz/Job-Portal`, and `cross-solution/YAWIK` all offer public GitHub codebases for self-hosted job publishing and candidate funnels.
+
+### Which open source recruiter tools are actually AI-native instead of just CRUD ATS apps?
+`Resume-Matcher`, `JobSync`, `acenji/ats`, `atscribe`, `next-hire-ai`, and `KalyanM45/Application-Tracking-System` are the most explicitly AI-oriented repositories in this list. Most other projects are better understood as infrastructure layers for recruiting operations.
+
+### Why are there fewer open source AI sourcing tools for recruiters than ATS tools?
+Because recruiter sourcing assistants often depend on proprietary data, browser automation, or external platform APIs. That pushes many vendors toward closed products, so the public GitHub ecosystem is still thinner than ATS and resume-analysis tooling.
