+## TL;DR
+- `srbhr/Resume-Matcher` is the strongest open-source AI resume tailoring tool in this niche, with a large community and active development.
+- `opencats/OpenCATS`, `Assystant/SpotAxis`, and `cross-solution/YAWIK` are the most useful open-source ATS-style foundations for recruiter workflows.
+- `OmkarPathak/pyresparser` and `xitanggg/open-resume` are strong building blocks for resume ingestion, parsing, and ATS-readability workflows.
+- `Riminder/open-jobboard`, `aschmelyun/laravel-job-board`, and `golang-cafe/job-board` are practical GitHub-hosted options for self-hosted job publishing.
+- Some subcategories, especially interview automation and recruiter sourcing assistants, still have fewer than 5 strong GitHub-native repos. Those gaps are noted honestly below.
+
+## Why This List
+For teams evaluating the best AI tools for recruiters in 2026, open source matters because hiring workflows touch resumes, candidate notes, interview data, and internal evaluation logic. A GitHub-first stack gives recruiters and talent-ops teams more control over privacy, customization, deployment, and long-term cost. It also makes due diligence easier: you can inspect the code, confirm the license, review maintenance activity, and decide whether a project is mature enough for production or better suited as a starting point.
