+## Contributing
+
+Contributions are welcome. Please keep submissions tightly scoped to this list's standard:
+
+- Every submission must include a public `github.com` repository URL.
+- No proprietary SaaS products will be accepted.
+- The project must be meaningfully useful for recruiters, recruiting operations, ATS workflows, resume parsing, hiring analytics, job boards, or candidate management.
+- Include stars, primary language, license, and last commit date from GitHub.
+- If a tool depends heavily on proprietary APIs or closed hosted services, explain that clearly in the PR.
+- If a category is still thin, document the gap honestly instead of padding the list with weak matches.
+
